# Carromscore environment variables (client-side, PUBLIC_* prefix means
# baked into the built bundle — do NOT put secrets here).
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in the values you need
# for local development. Production/beta reads the same names via
# GitHub Actions repo secrets.

# ─── Admin bootstrap ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# One-time self-promotion aid for the first super-admin.
#
# The RTDB rule at /adminRoles/$uid permits an authenticated user to
# write their own super-role entry ONLY when the /adminRoles node is
# completely empty. So the very first sign-in on a fresh Firebase
# project can promote itself.
#
# `bootstrapSuperIfNeeded()` in src/lib/roles.ts guards that
# self-promotion write on the client side by requiring the signed-in
# UID to match PUBLIC_BOOTSTRAP_SUPER_UID. This is a client-side
# convenience — the rule itself is still the security boundary.
#
# To find your UID: sign in with Google (via the lobby's sign-in pill
# or the home footer "Admin" link), open the account menu, tap
# "Copy UID". Paste it below, redeploy, then sign in again — the
# bootstrap fires and writes /adminRoles/<yourUid> = "super".
#
# Once a super exists, this variable becomes a no-op (the rule closes
# the bootstrap door).
PUBLIC_BOOTSTRAP_SUPER_UID=
